      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Still hoping for this. A PhysBone setting to only add motion if the direct parent gains offsets would allow for better props. Even if a PhysBone is nested in the armature, it will move when the avatar turns, which is undesirable in many cases.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-05-18T02:41:02.554Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Currently when you set the PhysBone immobile setting to \"World\" and max out the value, the motion from the root bone is not affected by avatar position changes, but it is affected by avatar rotation changes. It would be useful if a PhysBone could be made to only be affected by the parent motion while ignoring all other avatar motion.",
